+# 0010. Record the product's architecture decisions beside the constitution
+
+Date: 2026-10-22
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+[`engineering-discipline.md`](../engineering-discipline.md#architecture-decision-records)
+sends every architecturally significant decision — structure, non-functional
+characteristics, dependencies, interfaces, construction techniques — to an ADR in
+this directory. The [index](README.md#what-belongs-in-this-directory) of this
+directory restricted it to records that constitute *a project*, generic enough to
+carry onto any domain. A decision about how the product itself is built — its
+build, its packages, its parsing, its reading — is architecturally significant and
+is not generic, so the two rules sent it to two different places, and no other home
+for it existed. A record that has no permitted home is either not written or written
+against a rule.
+
+## Decision
+
+We will keep the product's own architecture decisions in this directory, in the one
+ADR sequence, with the same format, linter and immutability as every other record.
+A **product record** decides how the product is built; a **constitutional record**
+decides how any project is run. Each product record says, in its Context, that it is
+a product record.
+
+A product record keeps rule 1 of the index: it references no issue or pull request.
+It may link, beyond the sibling constitutive documents, to the product's own
+requirements ([`prd/`](../prd/)), specification ([`spec/`](../spec/)) and facts
+([`facts/`](../facts/)), which travel with the product. It keeps rule 2 and never
+links into the closed archive.
+
+We reject a second directory for product records, which would split the single ADR
+sequence and its linter in two, and we reject keeping product decisions out of ADRs,
+which would leave the structure of the product undecided on paper.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A copy of this repository onto another domain keeps the constitutional records and
+  drops the product records; the Context line of each record says which it is.
+- The index of this directory and
+  [`engineering-discipline.md`](../engineering-discipline.md#architecture-decision-records)
+  name both kinds of record.
+- A decision that has more than one option surviving the filter is not an ADR yet:
+  it stays a section "Decision pending the bet" in the architecture under
+  [`spec/`](../spec/) until the bet picks one.
