+# 0011. Build tally with go build only
+
+Date: 2026-10-22
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+This is a product record ([ADR-0010](0010-record-product-architecture-decisions.md)).
+tally is built with the Go toolchain and needs no other build tool
+([NFR-020](../prd/PRD-0001-tally.md), F-0003#3), in Go with the standard library
+only (NFR-018, NFR-019). Two options were filtered against the requirements, the
+facts, the invariants of [`guardrails.md`](../guardrails.md) and ADR-0001 to
+ADR-0009: `go-build-only` and `make-wrapper`.
+
+## Decision
+
+We will build tally with the commands of the Go toolchain alone: `go build` builds
+the binary and `go test` runs the tests, with no build file of another tool. The
+architecture is [SPEC-0002](../spec/SPEC-0002-tally-architecture.md).
+
+We reject `make-wrapper`, a Makefile around the Go commands: it fails NFR-020 and
+fact F-0003#3, because building then needs a tool other than the Go toolchain.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A clone builds wherever Go is installed, with no other tool.
+- The exact Go command of each test level is still the team's to name in
+  [`test-levels.md`](../tests/test-levels.md); this record names none.
