+# 0012. Count with three functions over a teed reader
+
+Date: 2026-10-22
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+This is a product record ([ADR-0010](0010-record-product-architecture-decisions.md)).
+The package `count` exports the functions that count the lines, the words and the
+characters of an `io.Reader`, and the command calls them
+([NFR-021](../prd/PRD-0001-tally.md), Q-010). Standard input can be read only once
+(REQ-008), and the peak heap for a 1 GiB file is at most 64 MiB (F-0003#24, Q-009).
+Three options were filtered: `three-functions-teed-reader`,
+`three-functions-reread-source` and `single-combined-function`.
+
+## Decision
+
+We will export three functions from the package `count` — one for the lines, one
+for the words and one for the characters — each over an `io.Reader`. The command
+reads each source once and feeds the same bytes to the three counts through a teed
+reader, so no source is read twice. The architecture is
+[SPEC-0002](../spec/SPEC-0002-tally-architecture.md).
+
+We reject `three-functions-reread-source`, which opens or reads the source once for
+each count: it fails REQ-008, because standard input cannot be read a second time.
+We reject `single-combined-function`, one exported function that returns the three
+counts: it fails NFR-021, which asks for the functions that count the lines, the
+words and the characters.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Each count has its own function to test, which serves the 90 percent coverage
+  target of the package `count`.
+- The teed reading must keep memory bounded: the three counts consume the bytes as
+  they flow, never a copy of the whole file ([ADR-0014](0014-stream-through-a-fixed-buffer.md)).
