+# 0015. Validate UTF-8 in the stream and print the row after the end of the file
+
+Date: 2026-10-22
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+This is a product record ([ADR-0010](0010-record-product-architecture-decisions.md)).
+A file that is not valid UTF-8 gets a message on standard error with its name and the
+exit code 1; it gets no row and adds nothing to the total; the other files are still
+counted, and rows already printed for earlier files stay
+([REQ-016](../prd/PRD-0001-tally.md), Q-003, Inv-3 of
+[`guardrails.md`](../guardrails.md)). A file is not text exactly when it is not valid
+UTF-8 (NFR-023, Q-007). Three options were filtered:
+`validate-in-stream-print-after-eof`, `print-row-while-reading` and
+`replace-invalid-with-fffd`.
+
+## Decision
+
+We will check that the bytes are valid UTF-8 while they stream through the buffer
+([ADR-0014](0014-stream-through-a-fixed-buffer.md)), and print a file's row only once
+the end of the file is reached with no invalid sequence. On the first invalid
+sequence tally stops reading that file, prints the message, adds nothing to the
+total and goes on with the next file. The architecture is
+[SPEC-0002](../spec/SPEC-0002-tally-architecture.md).
+
+We reject `print-row-while-reading`, which writes the row before the whole file is
+checked: it fails Inv-3, because an invalid byte found late would follow a row
+already printed. We reject `replace-invalid-with-fffd`, which counts each invalid
+sequence as U+FFFD: it fails NFR-023, fact F-0003#11 and Inv-3, because it counts a
+file that is not text.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- One pass over each file both validates and counts it; no file is read twice.
+- A file's counts are held until its end, so the total adds only files found valid.
